{
  "id": "ep206",
  "duration": 53.474,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.507,
      "text": "We purposely crashed a spacecraft straight into a fast-moving asteroid.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Dart-poster3.jpg",
        "credit": "Credits: NASA/Johns Hopkins Applied Physics Lab",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dart-poster3.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.433,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 2.433,
          "end": 4.5,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.507,
      "end": 13.677,
      "text": "Launched in November 2021, the DART mission targeted Dimorphos, a small moonlet orbiting Didymos seven million miles from Earth.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Dimorphos North-Up Image Composition reduced bloom.png",
        "credit": "NASA/Johns Hopkins APL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dimorphos_North-Up_Image_Composition_reduced_bloom.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.5,
          "end": 9.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 9.067,
          "end": 13.667,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 13.677,
      "end": 22.022,
      "text": "Traveling at roughly 14,000 miles per hour, the probe used onboard autonomous navigation to lock onto its target.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Webb Captures DART Impact (weic2215c).jpeg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, CSA, and STScI",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Webb_Captures_DART_Impact_(weic2215c).jpeg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 13.667,
          "end": 22.033,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 22.022,
      "end": 31.492,
      "text": "On September 26, 2022, the impact was photographed by the Italian CubeSat LICIACube alongside Hubble and James Webb.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Hubble captures DART asteroid impact debris (annotated 1) (heic2302a).tiff",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, STScI, J. Li (PSI)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hubble_captures_DART_asteroid_impact_debris_(annotated_1)_(heic2302a).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 22.033,
          "end": 31.5,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 31.492,
      "end": 38.312,
      "text": "Scientists originally hoped the violent collision would shorten the moonlet orbit by just 73 seconds.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 31.5,
          "end": 38.3,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 38.312,
      "end": 47.037,
      "text": "Instead, massive debris plumes acted like a rocket engine and punched the rock so hard it shortened the orbit by 32 minutes.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "This chart offers insight into data the DART team used to determine the orbit of Dimorphos after impact.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/Johns Hopkins APL/Astronomical Institute of the Academy of Sciences of the Czech Republic/Lowell Observatory/JPL/Las Cumbres Observatory/Las Campanas Observatory/European Southern Observatory Dan",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:This_chart_offers_insight_into_data_the_DART_team_used_to_determine_the_orbit_of_Dimorphos_after_impact.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 38.3,
          "end": 47.033,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 47.037,
      "end": 53.124,
      "text": "That massive planetary defense success proved we can alter the path of a fast-moving asteroid.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Dart-poster3.jpg",
        "credit": "Credits: NASA/Johns Hopkins Applied Physics Lab",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dart-poster3.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 47.033,
          "end": 53.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
